[:option {:value "925361"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "925363"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "925368"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "925370"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "925375"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "925380"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "925382"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "16000000"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "30915"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "30923"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "30936"} "1936"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/372"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Polo, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "18 – 21 June 1908"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/222"} "Hurlingham Polo Grounds, London"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/30909"} "12 from 1 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The Olympic matches had little relevance in the overall context of the 1908 international polo season.  From May to August, there was a non-stop round of tournaments in such fashionable places as London, Paris, Ostend, and Cannes, and Olympic polo held no special place in this social and sporting calendar.  Fewer than 30 high-handicapped players formed the core of the variously styled teams who played both with and against each other throughout the summer, and all the Olympic players had been both teammates and opponents in recent weeks."] "\n\n" [:p {} "For the Olympic tournament, an entry of only three teams, two from England and one from Ireland, meant that just two matches were played.  The English teams entered under the names of their respective clubs, and it was appropriate that the brothers " [:a {:href "/athletes/17977"} "Charles"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/17978"} "George Miller"] ", who owned and founded the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/16578"} "Roehampton Club"] ", were on the winning team.  Contrary to certain reports, this was not a round-robin tournament.  The Irish team never played at Hurlingham and qualified for the final by drawing a bye in the first round.  The winning Roehampton team was awarded the Hurlingham Trophy, in addition to their gold medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Roehampton"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/17978"} "George Miller"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/17979"} "Patteson Nickalls"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/17984"} "Herbert Wilson"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/17977"} "Charles Miller"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=2"] [:td {} "Ireland"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/17972"} "Hardress Lloyd"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/17974"} "John McCann"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/17983"} "Auston Rotheram"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/17981"} "Percy O'Reilly"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=2"] [:td {} "Hurlingham"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td 